            "id": "4949784",
            "title": "Top Growth Stocks For A Post-Seasonal Market And Midterms Boost",
            "description": "<html><body><figure class=\"getty-figure\" data-type=\"getty-image\"><picture> <img alt=\"growth in business and finance, growing graphs and charts\" data-id=\"1795167728\" data-type=\"getty-image\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"1024\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 132px), (max-width: 1199px) calc(100vw - 666px), (max-width: 1307px) calc(100vw - 708px), 600px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1795167728/image_1795167728.jpg?io=getty-c-w630\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1795167728/image_1795167728.jpg?io=getty-c-w1536 1536w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1795167728/image_1795167728.jpg?io=getty-c-w1280 1280w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1795167728/image_1795167728.jpg?io=getty-c-w1080 1080w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1795167728/image_1795167728.jpg?io=getty-c-w750 750w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1795167728/image_1795167728.jpg?io=getty-c-w640 640w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1795167728/image_1795167728.jpg?io=getty-c-w480 480w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1795167728/image_1795167728.jpg?io=getty-c-w320 320w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1795167728/image_1795167728.jpg?io=getty-c-w240 240w\" width=\"1536\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"> </p> <p class=\"item-credits\">anyaberkut/iStock via Getty Images</p></figcaption></figure> <h2>Top Growth and Momentum Stocks vs. Macro Headwinds</h2> <p data-eci=\"true\">The seasons are changing in more ways than one: Autumn is here, reminding investors that Q4 and the end of market seasonality are just around the calendar corner, while U.S. midterm elections are less than six<span class=\"paywall-full-content\"> weeks away. The market sent a clear bullish signal this week as the Nasdaq Composite index surged 2% in a single session on Monday to reach a new all-time high, a level more than 30% above its low set in March. The tech-heavy index leads the S&amp;P 500, which sits roughly 1% below its record, signaling that July’s AI and broader tech selloff was a potential reset favoring growth and momentum. That said, sentiment remains cautious, with CNN's Fear and Greed index still registering “Fear.” At the same time, this may also signal a contrarian tailwind, suggesting short-term weakness can be considered a buying opportunity.</span></p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure paywall-full-content\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"Fear &amp; Greed Index - Investor Sentiment\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"316\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698232799675.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698232799675.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698232799675.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698232799675.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"632\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>CNN.com</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"paywall-full-content\">Meanwhile, oil is creeping higher after falling roughly 15% as Middle East tensions fluctuate. The benchmark 10-year Treasury yield has also surged above 5.10% as bond investors observed a weaker-than-expected five-year Treasury <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4646269-us-5-year-treasury-note-auction-pays-highest-yield-since-2006\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4646269-us-5-year-treasury-note-auction-pays-highest-yield-since-2006\">auction</a> on Wednesday. All this serves as a reminder that volatility can still be expected in the weeks ahead, but markets are approaching the end of their historically weaker seasonal trends. And looking toward midterms, the S&amp;P 500 has averaged a <a href=\"https://www.schwab.com/learn/story/what-2026-midterms-could-mean-markets\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://www.schwab.com/learn/story/what-2026-midterms-could-mean-markets\">12.4% gain</a> during the six months following these elections since 1974.</p> <p class=\"paywall-full-content\">Against this backdrop, Quant Strong Buy stocks that combine high growth and momentum factor grades can provide a good starting point for stock selection.</p> <h2 class=\"paywall-full-content\">How I Chose the Top Growth Stocks With Momentum</h2> <p class=\"paywall-full-content\">To arrive at my top three growth stocks with momentum as the market transitions out of seasonality and through the midterms, I started with the Seeking Alpha stock screener. I then chose the pre-screen list of <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/screeners/9679348d-Top-Growth-Stocks\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/screeners/9679348d-Top-Growth-Stocks\">top growth stocks</a> and chose the strong buys with 'A-' or higher growth and momentum grades while avoiding duplication in any single sector to allow for diversification.</p> <h3 class=\"paywall-full-content\">1. Micron Technology, Inc. (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU\" title=\"Micron Technology, Inc.\">MU</a>)</h3> <ul class=\"paywall-full-content\"> <li><p>Market Capitalization: $1.22T</p></li> <li><p>Quant Rating: Strong Buy</p></li> <li><p>Quant Sector Ranking (As of Sept. 24, 2026): 1 out of 534</p></li> <li><p>Quant Industry Ranking (As of Sept. 24, 2026): 1 out of 71</p></li> <li><p>Sector: Information Technology</p></li> <li><p>Industry: Semiconductors</p></li> </ul> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure paywall-full-content\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"MU Stock Factor Grades\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"173\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698232743676.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698232743676.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"267\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"paywall-full-content\">Micron Technology provides the most direct exposure to the AI infrastructure buildout among my three growth and momentum selections, but its attraction extends beyond just the “pick-and-shovel” narrative. Surging demand for high-bandwidth memory and DRAM has produced huge earnings growth, while limited industry supply amid high demand supports pricing and increasing profit margins. Analysts expect MU’s upcoming earnings to mark a third consecutive quarter of triple-digit revenue growth, accompanied by another significant increase in earnings. MU shares have responded accordingly, rising more than 280% year-to-date, approaching a 45% gain off the July low. This combination of accelerating fundamentals and powerful price performance provides an outstanding demonstration of how growth and momentum can complement each other.</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure paywall-full-content\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"MU Stock Growth Metrics\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"737\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-1790269823428488.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-1790269823428488.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-1790269823428488.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-1790269823428488.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"609\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"paywall-full-content\">It’s not often that I see ‘A+’ grades for so many key metrics, and Micron’s <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU/growth\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU/growth\">growth scorecard</a> is one of those rarities. MU’s forward GAAP EPS is expected to grow at more than 510%, which is more than 25x the tech sector median, as strong memory demand and pricing power translate to fast-growing profitability. Meanwhile, Forward Operating Cash Flow Growth is expected at more than 175%, approaching 10x the sector’s 18.26%, as revenue growth flows through the business.</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure paywall-full-content\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"MU Stock Performance Momentum\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"258\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-1790270128323046.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-1790270128323046.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-1790270128323046.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-1790270128323046.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"545\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"paywall-full-content\">Micron’s dip in its three-month <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU/momentum/performance\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU/momentum/performance\">performance</a> reflects the steep July AI selloff, which pushed MU’s price down nearly 40%, but the sector-crushing longer-term returns support the company’s ‘A+’ Momentum Factor grade. Considering Micron’s fundamental strength, including a growth-adjusted forward <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU/valuation/metrics\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU/valuation/metrics\">PEG of 0.08</a> that suggests a 93% discount to the sector, MU has more room to run higher in an environment supporting growth stocks.</p> <p class=\"paywall-full-content\">My next stock selection expands the theme, combining cloud computing with one of the world’s dominant retail businesses, as well as a solid history of Q4 performance.</p> <h3 class=\"paywall-full-content\">2. Amazon.com, Inc. (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AMZN\" title=\"Amazon.com, Inc.\">AMZN</a>)</h3> <ul class=\"paywall-full-content\"> <li><p>Market Capitalization: $2.69T</p></li> <li><p>Quant Rating: Strong Buy</p></li> <li><p>Quant Sector Ranking (As of Sept. 24, 2026): 2 out of 478</p></li> <li><p>Quant Industry Ranking (As of Sept. 24, 2026): 1 out of 28</p></li> <li><p>Sector: Consumer Discretionary</p></li> <li><p>Industry: Broadline Retail</p></li> </ul> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure paywall-full-content\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"AMZN Stock Factor Grades\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"177\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-1790269823400113.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-1790269823400113.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"277\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"paywall-full-content\">Amazon offers multiple growth engines as the market enters the fourth quarter. AMZN’s<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4622393-amazon-outlines-q3-net-sales-of-197b-202b-while-lifting-2026-cash-capex-to-about-220b\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4622393-amazon-outlines-q3-net-sales-of-197b-202b-while-lifting-2026-cash-capex-to-about-220b\"> Q2 revenue</a> increased 20% year-over-year to $200.6 billion, while operating income surged 43%. AWS growth accelerated to nearly 37%, its fastest pace in 18 quarters, while advertising revenue increased 26%. The combination of cloud computing, AI, advertising, and e-commerce gives Amazon considerably more diversified growth drivers than a pure AI infrastructure stock. The timing may also prove favorable as Prime Big Deal Days, <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/primebigdealdays\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://www.amazon.com/primebigdealdays\">the next</a> of which is Oct. 6-7, followed by Black Friday, Cyber Monday, and holiday shopping, providing potential boosts as 2026 <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4645903-seven-consumer-discretionary-stocks-with-long-running-strong-buy-quant-ratings\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4645903-seven-consumer-discretionary-stocks-with-long-running-strong-buy-quant-ratings\">consumer spending</a> remains robust.</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure paywall-full-content\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"AMZN Stock Growth Metrics\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"735\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698233943284.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698233943284.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698233943284.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698233943284.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"613\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"paywall-full-content\">Amazon’s 14.10% forward revenue growth is more than 3x the sector median, while forward operating cash flow growth of 28.54%, which is also over 3x the sector, indicates AMZN is maintaining its strong underlying cash generation, increasing its self-funding capacity. This leads to the company’s negative year-over-year Levered FCF, which is largely a result of Amazon’s massive infrastructure capex that can be beneficial going forward if AWS continues its acceleration.</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure paywall-full-content\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"AMZN Stock Price Momentum\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"261\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902703337679257.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902703337679257.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902703337679257.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"430\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"paywall-full-content\">AMZN’s <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AMZN/momentum/performance\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AMZN/momentum/performance\">performance</a> shows consistency across every period Quant measures, and it demonstrates outstanding resilience as it produces mostly double-digit returns while the sector median has been mostly negative. This performance supports AMZN’s solid ‘A-’ Momentum Factor Grade.</p> <p class=\"paywall-full-content\">My third and final featured stock demonstrates how strong growth and momentum aren’t limited to mega-cap technology or consumer discretionary stocks.</p> <h3 class=\"paywall-full-content\">3. Flotek Industries, Inc. (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/FTK\" title=\"Flotek Industries, Inc.\">FTK</a>)</h3> <ul class=\"paywall-full-content\"> <li><p>Market Capitalization: $1.05B</p></li> <li><p>Quant Rating: Strong Buy</p></li> <li><p>Quant Sector Ranking (As of Sept. 24, 2026): 1 out of 288</p></li> <li><p>Quant Industry Ranking (As of Sept. 24, 2026): 1 out of 40</p></li> <li><p>Sector: Materials</p></li> <li><p>Industry: Specialty Chemicals</p></li> </ul> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure paywall-full-content\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"FTK Stock Factor Grades\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"178\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698234225068.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902698234225068.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"269\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"paywall-full-content\">Flotek Industries shifts the growth and momentum theme into the materials sector through a specialty chemicals and data analytics business that offers diverse exposure to energy, power, and infrastructure. Its growth trajectory and expanding backlog have been impressive, as <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4627077-flotek-outlines-340m-350m-2026-revenue-and-47m-51m-adjusted-ebitda-as-puerto-rico-deal-adds\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4627077-flotek-outlines-340m-350m-2026-revenue-and-47m-51m-adjusted-ebitda-as-puerto-rico-deal-adds\">FTK’s Q2</a> was its strongest quarterly performance in the last 10 years. Flotek management now expects $340-$350 million in annual revenue and $47-$51 million in adjusted EBITDA. Expanding international chemistry sales and accelerating data analytics business provide additional fundamental support.</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure paywall-full-content\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"FTK Stock Growth Metrics\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"442\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902704461924584.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902704461924584.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902704461924584.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902704461924584.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"542\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"paywall-full-content\">Further demonstrating FTK’s top line and fundamental operating strength, its forward revenue growth of more than 28% is more than 4x the sector median, an outstanding feat for a small-cap company. Even more impressive is the forward EBITDA growth of more than 46%, which compares to 9.45% for materials sector peers, demonstrating that Flotek’s sales are translating into significant profitability and that the growth story can continue.</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure paywall-full-content\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"FTK Stock Price Momentum\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"260\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902704931098793.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902704931098793.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902704931098793.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/24/50113560-17902704931098793.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"545\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"paywall-full-content\">FTK’s recent performance, which earns it an ‘A+’ Quant <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/FTK/momentum/performance\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/FTK/momentum/performance\">Momentum Grade</a>, includes a nearly 75% surge following its stellar Q2 earnings but also a steep decline, nearly giving all those gains back amid risk-off sentiment in July. This selloff provides an opportunity for aggressive investors to buy shares as growth and momentum potential returns.</p> <p class=\"paywall-full-content\">FTK demonstrates how screening for key quant factors like growth and momentum can uncover opportunities beyond the market’s largest technology names like MU and AMZN, taking us to our broader takeaways for investors.</p> <h2 class=\"paywall-full-content\">Conclusion: Focusing on Growth and Momentum Stocks</h2> <p class=\"paywall-full-content\">Markets entering a new phase as they approach and surpass record highs can require a different approach than markets recovering from sharp declines. Rather than simply buying beaten-down stocks, investors can focus on companies where improving fundamentals are being confirmed by strong growth and price momentum. MU, AMZN, and FTK provide three different examples, ranging from semiconductors to consumer and cloud computing to specialty chemicals and data analytics. Their diverse business models also reduce reliance on any single market segment. Macroeconomic headwinds may remain in place well into 2027, and volatility is to be expected. However, I remain bullish that broader growth trends can also stay in place, making temporary weakness a potential buying opportunity for high-quality stocks with strong quant growth and momentum metrics.</p> <p class=\"paywall-full-content\">We have many stocks with strong buy recommendations, and you can filter them using <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/screeners#hasComeFromMpArticle=true#source=section%3Amain_content%7Cbutton%3Abody_link\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/screeners#hasComeFromMpArticle=true#source=section%3Amain_content%7Cbutton%3Abody_link\">stock screens</a>